    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@/~cl_13__para_a",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "a",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@/~cl_13",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by inserting after subsection (2) the following subsection: “(2A) A vocational licence issued under this Part shall be valid for the period specified in the vocational licence unless it is sooner revoked under subsection (4) or (4A).”;"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@/~cl_13__para_b",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "b",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@/~cl_13",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in paragraph (4)(a), by inserting after the words “any disease” the words “, conduct as may be prescribed”; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@/~cl_13__para_c",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "c",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@/~cl_13",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by inserting after subsection (4) the following subsection: “(4A) Without prejudice to subsection (4), a vocational licence issued under this Part shall— (a) be suspended if the driving licence issued under section 27 is suspended under section 32, 35 or 36; (b) be revoked if the driving licence issued under section 27 is revoked under section 35.”. Amendment of section 59"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@/~cl_14",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "14",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Subsection 59(9) of the principal Act is amended by substituting for the words “not exceeding two thousand” the words “of not less than three hundred ringgit and not more than two thousand”. Amendment of section 66A"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@/~cl_15",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "15",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Subsection 66A(2) of the principal Act is amended by substituting for the words “not exceeding five thousand” the words “of not less than three hundred ringgit and not more than five thousand”. New section 76A"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@/~cl_16",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "16",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2012/29/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The principal Act is amended by inserting after section 76 the following section: “Authorized left turns 76A. (1) Notwithstanding a red signal or other traffic sign indicating a place where traffic must stop at any traffic junction, any person driving a motor vehicle on a road may turn left at the traffic junction in accordance with any traffic sign authorizing such left turn that has been lawfully sited on such road after stopping before the marked stop line on the road to ascertain that it is safe to do so. (2) For the purpose of subsection (1), the Minister may, after consultation with the Minister charged with the responsibility for works, make rules relating to the movement of motor vehicles and pedestrians and the erection of traffic signs at such authorized left turn traffic junctions. (3) An appropriate authority may, with the approval of the Minister charged with the responsibility for works in relation to a Federal road and designated Federal Territory road, and in any case after consultation with the Chief Police Officer, establish such traffic signs as it considers appropriate, and shall execute any works (including the placing, erection and maintenance of traffic signs) required in connection with such authorized left turn traffic junctions. (4) Any person who contravenes this section or any rules made under this section in relation to an authorized left turn shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be liable to a fine of not less than three hundred ringgit and not more than two thousand ringgit.”. Amendment of section 79"
      }
    },
